d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Addressed in the same rewrite as allstar-sleepy-armadillo (Gerrit 3480, commit 2b5e23a32c0): the test no longer uses future.result(timeout=60); workers are joined without a per-worker bound and the suite's 300 s per-test budget bounds a hang. Not yet done for this ticket: a deterministic reproduction of the 60 s expiry (observed 2 of 2 serial runs at load 25-45, 203 s and 247 s wall); it stays open until that is recorded or the bug is closed against 3480 with that evidence.","timestamp":1795183889600922001}],"created_at":1795181752771218001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"eee8a8d3-f06d-4c6f-9475-79e2b142f131","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fa59-9a21-097b-49be"}],"description":"## Observation\nOutside the agent sandbox on 2026-11-20 at about 06:00 PST (host load average 25-45 from concurrent verifies), `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py::test_two_processes_publish_at_most_one_equivalent_same_ticket_bundle` failed 2 of 2 serial runs with `concurrent.futures.TimeoutError` from `future.result(timeout=60)` (test line 401), after 247 s and 203 s of wall time. Each of the 2 `ProcessPoolExecutor` workers starts a fresh interpreter, imports rebar, and commits a completion bundle through git.\n\nInside the sandbox the same test fails earlier for a different reason, filed as allstar-sleepy-armadillo.\n\n## Hypothesis (unproven)\nThe 60 s per-future bound is a wall-clock assumption about worker start-up and git latency that a loaded host violates; it adds no hang protection beyond the suite's 300 s per-test budget, because leaving the `with ProcessPoolExecutor` block still waits for the workers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic reproduction (for example a git shim adding a fixed delay per start inside the workers) is recorded here.\n- [ ] The test no longer depends on a hard-coded worker wall-clock bound, with the reproduction passing.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","fa59-9a21-097b-49be"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9b8a-60c3-2194-418c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_two_processes_publish_at_most_one_equivalent_same_ticket_bundle waits only 60 s for its worker processes","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["49010023-6cba-4743-b755-91536522d814","eee8a8d3-f06d-4c6f-9475-79e2b142f131","d102f4c7-46d1-4833-8461-2cdb6d03f06d"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795183889600922002,"uuid":"9d50b96e-414f-4e0a-af56-def972617b87"}